  "removals": [
    {
      "target": "~",
      "cwd": "/home/user/project",
      "home": "/home/user",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "ask",
        "message": "Dangerous rm operation detected: '/home/user'\n\nThis command would remove a critical system directory. This requires explicit approval and cannot be auto-allowed by permission rules.",
        "reason": "on critical path: /home/user"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "~/project",
      "cwd": "/home/user/project",
      "home": "/home/user",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "ask",
        "message": "Dangerous rm operation detected: '/home/user/project'\n\nThis command would remove a workspace directory (the working directory, an additional working directory, or one of their parent directories). This requires explicit approval and cannot be auto-allowed by permission rules.",
        "reason": "on working directory or its ancestor: /home/user/project"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "~/project/*",
      "cwd": "/home/user/project",
      "home": "/home/user",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "ask",
        "message": "Dangerous rm operation detected: '/home/user/project/*'\n\nThis command would remove a workspace directory (the working directory, an additional working directory, or one of their parent directories). This requires explicit approval and cannot be auto-allowed by permission rules.",
        "reason": "on working directory or its ancestor: /home/user/project/*"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "~/build/*",
      "cwd": "/home/user/project",
      "home": "/home/user",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "passthrough",
        "message": "No dangerous removals detected for rm command"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "~/build",
      "cwd": "/home/user/project",
      "home": "/home/user",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "passthrough",
        "message": "No dangerous removals detected for rm command"
      }
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows patterns isolate the platform/NT namespace branches; UNC trust predicates are fixed false.",
    "Removal probes inject a POSIX path/critical-directory/filesystem provider with no symlinks or additional working directories and no mounted-drive rule. The artifact's tilde-expansion and removal branch order are executed; executable dispatch and shell expansion are not run."
  ]
